From: JoshuaHayesWasHere <josh.hayes121@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:22:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(web): jstack tree roots step down in size, every
 project is a root row, No project pinned last

Root rows are 36px at 15/650 with 10px above, homes 28px at 13/450 and 90% ink,
workers 24px at 12/400 and 70% ink, so a project no longer reads as one of its homes.
The two off-scale sizes are theme tokens, text-tree-root and text-tree-home.
A project with no jstack home draws through the same root row over its threads, and
the separate folder row goes. T3's "No project" group never takes a home and is
pinned last, faded while idle.
